/src/ladb_opencutlist/html/dialog-*.html
/src/ladb_opencutlist/css/ladb-opencutlist.css
/src/ladb_opencutlist/css/ladb-opencutlist.min.css
/src/ladb_opencutlist/css/ladb-opencutlist-icons.min.css
/src/ladb_opencutlist/css/lib/*.min.css
/src/ladb_opencutlist/css/vendor.min.css
# The dialog's JS bundles. Built by gulp, so normally ignored, and taken from
# dist/ladb_opencutlist.rbz by tools/mcft-refresh-outputs.sh — EXCEPT the tabs
# bundle, which is tracked on the mcft line on purpose.
#
# On OpenCutList 8 the tabs dialog loads THREE files: common-bundle.js,
# tabs-bundle.js and js/i18n/<lang>.js. tabs-bundle.js concatenates every tab
# plugin (tab-cutlist.js, which carries the MCFT estimate, among them) and the
# compiled twig templates. The rbz's copy is stock 8's, so without this
# exception MOP's Ruby would load and the estimate slide would not be there,
# with nothing saying why (docs/mcft/MOP-ON-OCL8.md §6.1).
#
# The /* form is load-bearing: git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# DIRECTORY is excluded, so `bundles/` followed by a `!` line is silently
# ignored. CI asserts both ways that the file is tracked and not ignored, and
# that it matches its sources.
/src/ladb_opencutlist/js/bundles/*
!/src/ladb_opencutlist/js/bundles/tabs-bundle.js
/src/ladb_opencutlist/js/templates/
/src/ladb_opencutlist/js/i18n/
/src/ladb_opencutlist/js/lib/three-orbit-controls.js
/src/ladb_opencutlist/js/lib/three-css-2d-renderer.js
/src/ladb_opencutlist/js/lib/three.js
/src/ladb_opencutlist/js/lib/bootstrap-slider.js
/src/ladb_opencutlist/bin/osx/lib/*
/src/ladb_opencutlist/bin/win/lib/*
/src/ladb_opencutlist/yaml/i18n/*
*~.skp
/build/node_modules/
/build/cmake-build/
/build/package-lock.json
# TRACKED on the mcft line: without it `npm ci` cannot run and the bundle CI
# rebuilds would be whatever the registry serves that day.
!/build/package-lock.json
/Gemfile.lock
/cmake-*
/tools/python/*.dxf
CLAUDE.md
.claude
.idea/

# SketchUp's own load-time artefacts, written INTO the extension folder.
#
# The Mac runs a dev install: Plugins/ladb_opencutlist is a symlink into this
# clone, so anything SketchUp writes beside the extension lands in the working
# tree and shows up as untracked for ever. Both of these are regenerated —
# they ship inside dist/ladb_opencutlist.rbz — so neither is source.
#
# Ignored UNANCHORED on purpose: the exact depth depends on how the symlink is
# placed and on the SketchUp version (2026 here), and a path-anchored rule
# would quietly stop matching the day either changes. That is the failure mode
# this repo keeps meeting — a check that silently stops checking.
#
# Amit, 2026-09-28, after the clone-sync check came back clean except for
# these two: "If they're regenerated each build, adding them to .gitignore
# would make this check come back completely clean."
extension_info.txt
*.susig

# tools/mcft-refresh-outputs.sh's stamp: which rbz the build outputs on disk
# came from, and a cksum of each. Written on the Mac, never source.
/src/ladb_opencutlist/.mcft-outputs*
